With a standardized C++ language we're in a much better starting
position than Rogue/Hack/Nethack had been at former times with C.
Machine depending details (e.g. size of data types) and platform
specific GUI aspekts would have to be considered anyway, similar
to the current code base, but all the OO languages can support a
design for significantly cleaner interfaces (low level and OS).

My doubts are whether one should use the existing NH code base,
or refactor the existing code into an OO framework, or build it
from scratch. All methods have their dis-/advantages.

